
The FindLeadIIMdl network was trained with the database PTB-XL [1-3], and we conducted the tight methodology (4GB VRAM, NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050) using CUDA 11.6, PyTorch 1.12.1, and fastai 1.0.61 (see Table S0), running locally. 
Our basis was this work [4] benchmarks, which utilized NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2080 Ti GPUs, are documented in the study's official GitHub repository.

STEPS:
1) git clone https://github.com/helme/ecg_ptbxl_benchmarking.git [4]. It's going to take time because it will download the dataset [1].
2) cd Documents/ecg_ptbxl_benchmarking/
2.1) cd code
3) Download my_codes_FindLeadIIRestMdl.zip. 
3.1) Copy the four .py files (at the code folder).
3.2) my_upload_to_5000.py is the main document.
3.3) To rewrite the path of the folder with the dataset [3].
  
For *.csv files:
4) Download the folder Reading_BIN.
4.1) Open the file Reading_my_BIN_file_12bits.m and rewrite the path of the folder with BIN files.
4.2) We already created the *.csv files for you as an example, but you can work with your benchmark.


